From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: fold 30 kernel-fixups into board patches (0173)

Folds every kernel-fixup that mutates fman_pcd.c/include/linux/fsl/
fman_pcd.h into a single board patch, in place of running them as
source-text mutations during every CI build. This is a pure
consolidation: the diff below is the exact, mechanically-captured net
effect of running these fixups in their real ci-setup-kernel.sh order
against the post-0172 tree. No logic was re-derived or guessed by hand.

Five of the thirty also touch other files as part of the same fixup
(F_069a.py: dpaa_eth.c: F_167.py: fman.c/fman.h; F_210.py/F_219.py/
F_211.py: fman_pcd_internal.h, and F_211.py also fman_pcd_kg.c). Their
contributions to those files are captured here too (applied in their
real relative order, verified to still apply cleanly against the
post-0172 state of those files), so removing their invocations doesn't
silently drop that part of their effect.

fman_pcd.c/fman_pcd.h were the two most heavily-mutated files in the
whole series -- 26 board patches and, before this fold, 46 separate
fixup mutations (72 total touches on fman_pcd.c alone). This fold
captures the fixups' cumulative NET effect (their real run order,
final state only) rather than re-deriving each one's intent by hand,
so it is correct regardless of whether any individual fixup in the
chain was itself later superseded by a subsequent one in the same
chain (the same class of trap as F-144/F-152 on this branch) -- that
churn, if any, is already resolved in the end state captured here.
This fold does not change what the kernel does, only how many places
that logic is scattered across.

Fixups folded (in application order): fe_flow_key_fix.py, three inline
mutate.py calls (F-085 debugfs __unused annotations + fe_flow key
pointer fix), F_069a.py, F_069b.py, F_071.py, two more inline mutate.py
calls (F-085b), F_134.py, F_135.py, F_136.py, M2_4_4.py, F_158.py,
F_167.py, F_169.py, F_171.py, F_172.py, F_188.py, F_189.py, F_193.py,
F_197.py, F_198.py, F_228.py, F_200.py, F_202.py, F_204.py, F_218.py,
F_220.py, F_221.py, F_225.py, F_210.py, F_219.py, F_211.py, F_226.py,
F_230.py, F_191.py.

Their bin/kernel-fixups/*.py files and ci-setup-kernel.sh invocations
are removed in the same commit as this patch, since their effect now
ships as part of the board patch series instead.

Verified: applies cleanly on top of 0172 against a pristine
linux-6.18.44 baseline; 119/119 patches apply; full kernel build
(Image + modules) compiles with 0 errors.
---
